WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:19.804
Hello . . . Who are you?

2
00:00:19.805 --> 00:00:23.454
I'm a Nile crocodile.

3
00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:27.578
We're the biggest reptiles on earth.

4
00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:30.425
Where do you live?

5
00:00:30.426 --> 00:00:34.599
Nile crocodiles live mostly in Africa.

6
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.800
We like warm swamps, rivers, and marshes.

7
00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.772
Your teeth look sharp!

8
00:00:42.773 --> 00:00:49.450
We have more than sixty teeth.

9
00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:52.665
But we can't chew with them.

10
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:57.675
We can only bite.

11
00:00:57.676 --> 00:01:00.189
What do you eat?

12
00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:04.450
We eat fish, turtles, and crabs.

13
00:01:04.451 --> 00:01:08.377
Our strong jaws open very wide.

14
00:01:08.378 --> 00:01:13.011
So we can eat zebras and hippos too.

15
00:01:13.012 --> 00:01:16.078
Are you dangerous?

16
00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:21.217
Yes! Nile crocodiles are very dangerous.

17
00:01:21.218 --> 00:01:25.767
Sometimes we eat people!

18
00:01:25.768 --> 00:01:28.552
Yikes!

19
00:01:28.553 --> 00:01:33.956
But Nile crocodiles are very caring parents.

20
00:01:33.957 --> 00:01:38.682
Most reptiles don't stay with their eggs.

21
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:44.766
We protect our eggs fiercely!

22
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.458
How do you swim?

23
00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:51.422
We use our powerful tails to move.

24
00:01:51.423 --> 00:01:55.626
Our eyes and ears stay above the water.

25
00:01:55.627 --> 00:02:00.428
That helps us see and hear.

26
00:02:00.429 --> 00:02:03.494
I'm ready for a swim now.

27
00:02:03.495 --> 00:02:05.772
Bye!

28
00:02:05.773 --> 00:02:15.039
Good-bye, Nile Crocodile.
